1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,348
A spreadsheet is the quickest way to fill or change a catalog, and

2
00:00:05,348 --> 00:00:07,582
a feed puts it in shopping ads.

3
00:00:07,582 --> 00:00:12,292
This video shows how to export and import products, how SKUs match rows,

4
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:16,580
how to move from another store, and how to publish product feeds.

5
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:25,346
Typing a hundred products one at a time is slow, and a spreadsheet

6
00:00:25,346 --> 00:00:27,950
is the format most stores already have.

7
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:34,240
Moving from Shopify or WooCommerce means moving a catalog, not retyping it.

8
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:39,726
Product import and export read and write a CSV file, with a column

9
00:00:39,726 --> 00:00:44,330
for each product detail, and match rows to your products by SKU.

10
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:50,143
A product feed publishes your products to Google, Meta and TikTok shopping, with

11
00:00:50,143 --> 00:00:52,380
the details those shops ask for.

12
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:02,960
Content Transfer adds Bulk Import and Bulk Export, for products like any other content.

13
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:05,572
Each product is a row.

14
00:01:05,572 --> 00:01:09,162
Its price, SKU, sale dates and more are columns.

15
00:01:09,162 --> 00:01:11,290
A template shows them all.

16
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:16,017
An export has the same columns, so you can change prices in a

17
00:01:16,017 --> 00:01:18,570
spreadsheet and import the file back.

18
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:24,731
Product Feeds publishes the catalog to shopping ads, and the Product Feed part

19
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:27,050
adds brand, GTIN and category.

20
00:01:31,253 --> 00:01:33,447
Open Content, Bulk Export.

21
00:01:33,447 --> 00:01:38,384
Choose the Product type and the CSV format, and click Export Data.

22
00:01:38,384 --> 00:01:41,263
The file has a row for each product.

23
00:02:02,388 --> 00:02:05,941
Change what you need in a spreadsheet, such as the prices.

24
00:02:05,941 --> 00:02:10,049
The file includes the content item id of each product, which is what

25
00:02:10,049 --> 00:02:12,158
lets an import update a product.

26
00:02:16,348 --> 00:02:21,343
Open Content, Bulk Import, click Import, and choose Product.

27
00:02:21,343 --> 00:02:25,808
Download template, CSV shows every column to fill in.

28
00:02:26,259 --> 00:02:27,586
Choose your file.

29
00:02:27,586 --> 00:02:33,006
Tick Publish imported content to publish the products as they come in, and click Upload.

30
00:02:33,006 --> 00:02:36,119
The import appears in the list, with its status.

31
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:40,865
Rows are matched to your products by SKU, so an import does not

32
00:02:40,865 --> 00:02:42,484
add a product twice.

33
00:02:42,484 --> 00:02:46,718
A row whose SKU an earlier row used is skipped, and the import

34
00:02:46,718 --> 00:02:48,710
says which row it repeats.

35
00:02:52,893 --> 00:02:56,987
With Product Feeds on, open Settings, Commerce, Product feeds.

36
00:02:56,987 --> 00:03:01,261
It shows the feed's address, how many products are in it, and why

37
00:03:01,261 --> 00:03:04,633
any are left out, such as a product with no photo.

38
00:03:05,084 --> 00:03:10,167
Set the default brand, the condition, a default Google product category, and whether

39
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:12,877
to include products that are out of stock.

40
00:03:12,877 --> 00:03:17,904
Give Google Merchant Center, Meta or TikTok the feed's address as a scheduled feed.

41
00:03:18,354 --> 00:03:22,719
The Product Feed part, added to a product type, adds a brand, a

42
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:27,401
GTIN, an MPN, a condition and a Google category to each product, and

43
00:03:27,401 --> 00:03:30,374
a way to keep a product out of the feeds.

44
00:03:34,574 --> 00:03:40,741
Export your products from Shopify or WooCommerce, and import the file as your product type.

45
00:03:40,741 --> 00:03:42,394
It is read as it is.

46
00:03:43,144 --> 00:03:47,662
Variants come in when the type has the Product variants part with options

47
00:03:47,662 --> 00:03:49,035
of the same names.

48
00:03:49,035 --> 00:03:53,324
Otherwise the product comes in as one product, from its lowest price.

49
00:03:54,074 --> 00:03:59,798
Categories and brands go to taxonomy fields named like Category and Brand, matched

50
00:03:59,798 --> 00:04:01,684
to their terms by name.

51
00:04:02,434 --> 00:04:04,424
Images are not downloaded.

52
00:04:04,424 --> 00:04:07,284
Add product photos in the media library.

53
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:12,700
A new catalog:

54
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:15,254
fill in the template, and import it.

55
00:04:16,004 --> 00:04:17,608
A price change:

56
00:04:17,608 --> 00:04:21,884
export, edit the prices, and import the file back.

57
00:04:22,634 --> 00:04:24,731
A move from another store:

58
00:04:24,731 --> 00:04:26,304
import its export.

59
00:04:27,054 --> 00:04:28,321
Shopping ads:

60
00:04:28,321 --> 00:04:31,854
publish a feed, and give its address to Google.

61
00:04:33,854 --> 00:04:37,176
Export, edit, import, and publish a feed.

62
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:39,014
Thanks for watching.

